# Build context for bench/Dockerfile (`docker build -f bench/Dockerfile .`).
.git
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
dist_tmp
bench/out
.bench-types
examples/laratype-test
.env
.env.*
# `.env*` at any depth: the root-only patterns above miss a nested file such as examples/basic/.env, which
# `COPY . .` would otherwise bake into the image. Docker's `**/` matches zero or more directories, so these also
# cover the root. No `.env.example` is tracked or read at build time, so no negation is needed.
**/.env
**/.env.*
.npmrc
.claude/
*.log
